{:edb/db-before-t 1109 :edb/db-after-t 1110 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534422 50 #inst "2026-10-07T02:27:33.618Z" 13194139534422 true] [17592186064164 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287442 13194139534422 true] [17592186064165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287449 13194139534422 true] [17592186064165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287453 13194139534422 true] [17592186064166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287456 13194139534422 true] [17592186064166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287460 13194139534422 true] [17592186287442 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287443 13194139534422 true] [17592186287442 1089 "q-15647" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287442 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534422 true] [17592186287442 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{3x+1}$ and the point $P(21,4)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$ calculate ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4).$" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287442 1113 #uuid "0c36b197-027f-56c2-a704-60e8c33c39b8" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287442 1145 "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(21,4).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt[3]{3x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{2/3}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(21) & =\\frac{1}{(64)^{2/3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(21,4)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(4,21)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$ \n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(21)} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287444 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287445 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287446 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287447 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287448 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1041 "selection" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287445 13194139534422 true] [17592186287443 1110 #uuid "3af8268c-56b5-5e72-85f4-2e16fa02fce9" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287444 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287444 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287444 1111 #uuid "9e06efb1-c614-5df4-a96d-54a8bc3e08a2" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287445 1034 "16" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287445 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287445 1111 #uuid "286f6836-e5cf-5ad9-91af-0d37c393b681" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287446 1034 "8" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287446 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287446 1111 #uuid "ef55e054-3b41-52ee-aef5-22ac31bec600" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287447 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287447 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287447 1111 #uuid "8494c0c2-11ad-5038-8e44-e8984fcbc27b" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287448 1034 "1" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287448 1111 #uuid "34f74688-ce7b-5d2e-ac6b-ba72b6e3921a" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287449 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287450 13194139534422 true] [17592186287449 1089 "q-342588" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287449 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534422 true] [17592186287449 1100 "Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(1)$ given the following table of values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $-2$ | $4$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $-7$ |\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287449 1113 #uuid "284514bc-fbdd-5962-b8a5-481ef5bc2a15" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287449 1145 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(1))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(1)=2$ and ${f}^{′}(2)=-7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-7)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287450 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287451 13194139534422 true] [17592186287450 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287452 13194139534422 true] [17592186287450 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534422 true] [17592186287450 1041 "field-1" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287450 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287452 13194139534422 true] [17592186287450 1110 #uuid "e1a287c1-3c09-5131-a2d0-07ea90edf310" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287451 1034 "7" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287451 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287451 1111 #uuid "b91cc901-d4a8-5750-bee2-35b539bb8889" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287452 1034 "-\\frac{1}{7}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287452 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287452 1111 #uuid "abf62472-d96a-5ca8-866a-dad158af934e" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287453 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287454 13194139534422 true] [17592186287453 1089 "q-342592" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287453 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534422 true] [17592186287453 1100 "Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)$ given the following table of values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $-8$ |\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287453 1113 #uuid "f0036795-b710-5f8f-94db-babdb3b4d3c9" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287453 1145 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(0)=2$ and ${f}^{′}(2)=-8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-8)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287455 13194139534422 true] [17592186287454 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534422 true] [17592186287454 1041 "field-1" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287454 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287455 13194139534422 true] [17592186287454 1110 #uuid "d62851f2-84e2-56c0-8a05-177da63414c4" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287455 1034 "-\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287455 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287455 1111 #uuid "93d6c80e-e791-55aa-b703-f982b38ee085" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287456 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287457 13194139534422 true] [17592186287456 1089 "q-342624" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287456 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534422 true] [17592186287456 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)={5}^{x}+3.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4).$\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287456 1113 #uuid "03828b42-335e-5615-88ca-ef552635348d" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287456 1145 "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(4).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(4)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(4) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =4 \\\\ {5}^{x}+3 & =4 \\\\ {5}^{x} & =1 \\\\ {5}^{x} & ={5}^{0} \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(4)=0.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={5}^{x}+3 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & ={5}^{0}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287457 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287458 13194139534422 true] [17592186287457 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287459 13194139534422 true] [17592186287457 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534422 true] [17592186287457 1041 "field-1" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287457 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287458 13194139534422 true] [17592186287457 1110 #uuid "933a8f66-b4f5-56c5-9264-4e3259c3756c" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287458 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\ln(5)}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287458 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287458 1111 #uuid "f5809f2a-705f-56ad-89df-26eff0e73638" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287459 1034 "5" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287459 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287459 1111 #uuid "9d4899d4-2b6e-5d3b-af50-d9fb3cd450ca" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287460 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287461 13194139534422 true] [17592186287460 1089 "q-342625" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287460 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534422 true] [17592186287460 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1).$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0).$\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287460 1113 #uuid "77a5f47e-8f48-52c6-b3b5-dcc98f89fccd" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287460 1145 "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(0).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(0)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(0) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(0)=2.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)+\\frac{x+3}{x-1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-1)+\\frac{2+3}{2-1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =0+5 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287461 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287462 13194139534422 true] [17592186287461 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534422 true] [17592186287461 1041 "field-1" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287461 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287462 13194139534422 true] [17592186287461 1110 #uuid "a93944aa-d827-5aa6-bd4d-ad8afdb1f5ad" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287462 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139534422 true] [17592186287462 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534422 true] [17592186287462 1111 #uuid "5a8647fa-d56d-55e8-86fd-f6210ac630a2" 13194139534422 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-15647" 17592186287442 "q-15647/selection" 17592186287443 "q-15647/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" 17592186287444 "q-15647/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" 17592186287445 "q-15647/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" 17592186287446 "q-15647/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" 17592186287447 "q-15647/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" 17592186287448 "q-342588" 17592186287449 "q-342588/field-1" 17592186287450 "q-342588/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" 17592186287451 "q-342588/field-1/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" 17592186287452 "q-342592" 17592186287453 "q-342592/field-1" 17592186287454 "q-342592/field-1/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f" 17592186287455 "q-342624" 17592186287456 "q-342624/field-1" 17592186287457 "q-342624/field-1/0f07028be0